## Objective

Turn the authoritative manufacturing preflight already delivered by #347 into a first-class SketchUp review workflow that explains blockers/warnings in user language and navigates each issue to the exact managed context without duplicating validation rules in Ruby or HtmlDialog.

Tracks #465 and #290.

## Mandatory authority

- `docs/architecture/sketchup-plugin-excellence.md`
- `docs/architecture/sketchup-authoring-interaction-contract.md`
- `docs/sketchup-excellence-execution-plan.md`
- `docs/sketchup-manufacturing-contract.md`
- `docs/architecture/sketchup-interaction-model.md`
- #347 authoritative preflight
- #346 semantic identity

## Baseline / problem

The plugin currently distinguishes interactive validation from a manufacturing badge, but the manufacturing result is not yet a complete review surface. Excellence requires:

```text
Run/refresh preflight
→ summary ready|warning|blocked
→ grouped issues
→ select issue
→ select/zoom/highlight owning furniture/part/hardware
→ show remediation
→ edit the relevant authoring intent
→ rerun/revalidate
```

The UI must never infer `ready` from local parameter validity.

## Required scope

### Preflight result adapter

Consume structured server/domain issues with at least:

- `code`;
- `message`;
- `severity`;
- `entityId` / identity path;
- semantic `path` where available;
- `remediation`;
- revision/fingerprint context when available.

Do not parse localized message strings to decide behavior.

### Review panel

Add a dedicated review experience that shows:

- overall state `ready | warning | blocked | stale | unavailable`;
- counts by severity;
- grouped issues by furniture and/or category;
- exact source context (mueble, part, hardware, relationship);
- remediation copy in Spanish;
- stale/offline/unavailable explicitly distinct from success.

### Viewport navigation

For a selected issue:

- resolve managed entity by Granete identity, not display name;
- select the most specific managed host entity available;
- recover owning FurnitureInstance via InstancePath/metadata when issue targets a child;
- frame/zoom/highlight without changing productive geometry;
- provide fallback navigation to owning furniture when the exact child was regenerated and host locator is stale.

### Fix loop

Where the issue can be corrected through existing authoring controls, expose context actions such as:

- `Seleccionar mueble`;
- `Seleccionar pieza`;
- `Editar material`;
- `Editar herraje` once #468 exists;
- `Revisar relación` when the direct-authoring flow from #467 supports the corresponding relationship intent.

Do not implement automatic domain fixes unless the server/domain explicitly exposes an approved command.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Local parameter validation can never mark manufacturing `ready`.
- [ ] A server `blocked` result is shown as blocking and prevents publish/release actions when those surfaces exist.
- [ ] Every issue with a valid `componentInstanceId` navigates to that managed child or its current regenerated equivalent.
- [ ] Hardware/relationship issues navigate to their host context without using names as identity.
- [ ] `remediation` is visible and actionable in Spanish.
- [ ] Stale/unavailable/offline are not rendered as green/ready.
- [ ] Rebuild that changes child `persistent_id` does not permanently break issue navigation when Granete identity remains valid.
- [ ] Re-running preflight refreshes issue state without duplicating business logic in the client.
- [ ] Selection/highlight/navigation itself does not mutate authoring/manufacturing state.
- [ ] Real-host TestUp covers at least one board issue and one hardware/relationship issue.

## Negative proof required

Tests must fail if:

- UI derives readiness only from `width/height/depth` bounds;
- localized error text controls severity/action;
- navigation matches by SketchUp name or geometry;
- a stale `persistent_id` makes a still-valid Granete entity unreachable without fallback;
- `unavailable` or network failure is presented as `ready`;
- preflight logic is reimplemented in Ruby/JavaScript.

## Suggested implementation areas

- `apps/sketchup-extension/src/granete_for_sketchup/ui/*`
- `apps/sketchup-extension/src/granete_for_sketchup/observers/*`
- preflight transport/adapter boundary
- `resources/dialog.html` or its successor UI modules
- host smoke fixtures

## Explicit non-goals

- deriving machining locally;
- editing derived holes directly;
- implementing Project DesignRevision persistence (#384);
- machine-specific postprocessing.

## Definition of Done

A blocked cabinet fixture can be reviewed entirely from SketchUp: the user sees why it is blocked, jumps to the exact managed context, applies an authoring correction through the appropriate editor, re-runs the authoritative preflight and reaches `ready` only when Granete returns it.

