## Shared foundations discovered during review

### #476 — SelectionContext

#466/#467/#468/#470/#471 all need one semantic selection/capability model. A nested shelf or hardware selection must retain exact Granete occurrence identity and owning furniture context across rename/rebuild.

### #477 — rich authoring resolve contract

The current layout boundary is optimized for dimensions/materials. Rich authoring must use one versioned structured request/response instead of proliferating `?shelf...` / `?hinge...` parameters. Before Gate A this can remain stateless authoritative resolution; it must not create Project business persistence.

## Organization Foundation / Digital Thread coordination

Host UX, stateless resolve, visualization, migration, performance and compatibility can progress before Gate A **only when they do not create a new persistent business family**.

Persistent Project `FurnitureInstance` / `Design` implementation follows #385 and waits for Gate A #462. No alternate SketchUp-only Project/Design aggregate, local shadow store or local server-authoritative ID scheme is allowed.

